          "id": "1772105655786",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1772105655788_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "Retrieve the following variables:\n\n- userAttributes from {{$context.$variables.employmentSession.userAttributes}}\n- infoNeededString from {{$context.$variables.employmentSession.infoNeededString}}\n\nProcessing Instructions:\n\n1. Examine the elements present in userAttributes.\n2. For EACH attribute present, include its corresponding table rendering section.\n3. If an attribute is NOT present in userAttributes, completely remove its entire section from infoNeededString.\n4. Do NOT merge attribute sections.\n5. If multiple attributes exist, render tables sequentially in the same order as userAttributes.\n6. Return the fully updated infoNeededString to the output variable.\n7. Do NOT output anything except the final updated infoNeededString.\n\n\n------------------------------------------------------------\nRENDERING RULES (Apply Separately for EACH Attribute)\n------------------------------------------------------------\n\nFor each attribute present:\n\n1) Display this instruction exactly:\n\nDisplay the following records for the attribute: <AttributeName>\n\n2) Above the table, display this title exactly:\n\nSelection Required for <AttributeName>\n\n3) Add spacing before and after each table using:\n\n\\n\\n\n\n4) Generate an left aligned HTML table with ONLY the following visible columns:\n\n1. Code\n2. Name\n\nDo NOT:\n- Create a row number column\n- Create or display any column named \"Hidden Fields\"\n- Display any sensitive or internal fields\n\nIf internal fields exist (such as Id, InternalId, PersonId, AssignmentId, etc.):\n- Include them as hidden input fields inside each table row\n- DO NOT create a visible column for them\n\nAlways display only:\n- The title text\n- The rendered HTML table\n- The closing instruction text\n\nNo raw HTML tags should be shown to the user.\n\n\n------------------------------------------------------------\nTABLE FORMATTING RULES\n------------------------------------------------------------\n\n- border: 2px solid black applied to table, th, and td\n- border-collapse: collapse\n- Header row text must be bold\n\n\n------------------------------------------------------------\nCLOSING TEXT (Below Each Table)\n------------------------------------------------------------\n\nPlease choose one record by providing the <AttributeName> Code\n\nThis text must NOT be part of the table.\n\n\n------------------------------------------------------------\nATTRIBUTE INCLUSION LOGIC\n------------------------------------------------------------\n\nIf userAttributes = [Job, BusinessUnit]:\n- Include BOTH BusinessUnit section and Job section.\n- Render BusinessUnit first (after normalization), then Job.\n\nIf userAttributes = [Job]:\n- Remove the entire BusinessUnit section completely.\n- Only render Job section.\n\nIf userAttributes = [BusinessUnit]:\n- Only render BusinessUnit section.\n\nIf additional attributes appear in userAttributes:\n- Apply the same rendering rules dynamically.\n\n\n------------------------------------------------------------\n\nFinal Step:\nReturn only the updated infoNeededString.\nDo not include explanations.\nDo not modify formatting text.\nDo not merge tables.\nDo not output anything else."
            },
            {
              "id": "1772105655786_systemPrompt",
              "name": "systemPrompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": ""
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n    \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n    \"type\": \"object\",\n    \"properties\": {\n        \"InfoNeededString\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n        }\n    }\n}",
          "type": "LLM"
        },
